></ul><p>That is fc1 + fc2 =3D 8,388,608 parameters.</p><p>For the GLU vari=
ant, we have</p><ul><li><p>fc1: 1024 =C3=97 1024 =3D 1,048,576</p></li><li>=
<p>fc2: 1024 =C3=97 1024 =3D 1,048,576</p></li><li><p>fc3: 1024 =C3=97 1024=
 =3D 1,048,576</p></li></ul><p>I.e., 3 =C3=97 1,048,576 =3D 3,145,728 weigh=
t parameters.</p><p>So, overall, using the GLU variants results in fewer pa=
rameters, and they perform better as well. The reason for this better perfo=
rmance is that these GLU variants provide an additional multiplicative inte=
raction, which improves expressivity (the same reason deep &amp; slim neura=
l nets perform better than shallow &amp; wide neural nets, provided they ar=
